<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    <!--
        Prerendering is disabled: the JWT lives in ProtectedSessionStorage, which needs JS
        interop that isn't available during prerendering (TokenStorageService treats that as
        "anonymous" — see its remarks). With prerendering on, a protected page briefly looks
        anonymous on every full page load, RedirectToLogin fires, the interactive circuit then
        sees the real (authenticated) state and bounces back with forceLoad — an infinite
        Dashboard <-> Login redirect loop, and stray full reloads mid-form-submit are also what
        triggers the "@formname" form-routing error. Skipping prerendering removes the whole
        window in which the auth state can disagree with itself.
    -->
    <Routes @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
